{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>Until the death of the High Priest.</b> And what the Torah stated concerning the killers, that he shall dwell there until the death of the High Priest — this is because Aaron's trait was peace; therefore it was incumbent upon him to pray for the people of his generation that only peace and truth should be in his days and that such an event, this untoward occurrence, should not befall them. Therefore he shall dwell there until the death of the High Priest, and then he and all his household will pray for the death of the High Priest, so that he may return speedily to his home. And for this reason it says: ״עַד מוֹת הַכֹּהֵן הַגָּדוֹל אֲשֶׁר מָשַׁח אוֹתוֹ בְּשֶׁמֶן הַקֹּדֶשׁ״ — but do we not yet know that the High Priest was anointed with the anointing oil? Rather, it is because this priest in whose days a murder was committed — this killer extinguished the lamp of Elohim, the soul of man, and extinguished the lamp of mitzvah, וְתוֹרָה אוֹר — surely this priest did not remember the holy anointing oil that was upon him, of which half was two hundred and fifty, that is, twice ״נֵר״, for every priest must stand to guard these two lamps in his days and to pray concerning this. And since this event happened in his days, therefore he shall dwell there until the death of the High Priest."], :book :numbers, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {0 "The wordplay on נֵר (lamp) and the numerical value 250 (נ=50, ר=200) depends on the phrase נֵר אֱלֹהִים נִשְׁמַת אָדָם (Proverbs 20:27) and נֵר מִצְוָה וְתוֹרָה אוֹר (Proverbs 6:23); twice נֵר = 500, matching the 500 holy shekels of the anointing oil ( Exodus 30:23–24), of which the component listed as חֲמִשִּׁים וּמָאתַיִם = 250 is highlighted. Translated hyper-literally where the argument hinges on numerical wordplay."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:44:06.161079843Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}